# Numa tone of voice

Source of truth: `docs/01-BRAND-VOICE.md`. Facts and what may be claimed: `docs/02-FACTS-AND-CLAIMS.md`. Execution brief: `docs/numa-change-log.md`. Do not use `docs/numa-tone-of-voice.md` or `13-BRAND-VOICE.md`.

**Clarity is never traded for voice.** A line that is on-voice but has to be decoded is not finished.

**Delivery is the only thing described as included.** If we are not obliged to offer it, it is complimentary.

**Named services, always capitalised.** Concierge unpacking. Adjust to Desire. Old mattress removal and recycling. Adjust to Desire never appears alone on first use: **Adjust to Desire.** A year to get the feel right. The verb is *adjust*. Never replacement, warranty claim, or a new layer we make.

**Three periods, three wordings.** No charge in the first 14 days. `{{ trial_nights }}` nights to return it. A year to get the feel right. The adjustment year is never counted in nights. Never `365 nights` or a `365 night comfort programme`.

**Never write "free".** Never mention anyone else. Never explain why you are good. State what happens.

**Numbers render as figures.** One rule.

**Never.** Exclamation marks. "Just", "simply", "easy". Title Case In Buttons And Headings. Scarcity. Emoji. Rhetorical questions in headlines. Staffing counts on delivery.

The test: read it aloud. If a first-time reader has to work it out, rewrite it.
